{
  "description": "#6755 — a tag's page is the page titled `Tag/<tag>` of its space, paired by that title under `name_key`. `create_tag_page` makes it or answers the one already there (a seeded `tag/Legacy` is adopted as spelled); every other create under `Tag/` and every rename of an ordinary page into the path is refused (`ReservedTagPageTitle`), `Tag` alone is ordinary, and a live tag's page does not leave the path. A tag and its page are renamed together, either from the tag or from the page, as two `edit_block`s in one transaction, undone together and reverted together from either half; onto a name another page or tag holds the rename is refused whole (`TagPageTitleTaken`). A deleted tag leaves its page, which may then leave the path. Re-author `expected` / `expected_ops` via CONFORMANCE_UPDATE=1.",
